## IMPLEMENTATION NOTES

1. Build as a SINGLE React component with default export.
2. Use useState for: activeSection, pipelineRunning, pipelineStage, 
   clickedRow, activeAudience, activeExportTab.
3. The pipeline animation uses setInterval to increment pipelineStage 
   from 0 to 6, with 800ms per stage. Show log lines appearing with 
   staggered setTimeout calls.
4. The spreadsheet row click shows a simple slide-in panel using 
   conditional rendering and Tailwind transition classes.
5. All charts use ResponsiveContainer with a fixed height (300px).
6. The sidebar is fixed-width (220px), content area takes remaining width.
7. Each section renders as a scrollable div.
8. Do NOT use localStorage or sessionStorage.
9. Do NOT use external images — use Lucide icons and coloured div blocks only.
10. Keep the file under 1000 lines by being concise in JSX. 
    Use helper functions for repeated patterns (StatCard, StageCard, etc.)

Make this beautiful, professional, and impressive for a government 
compliance demo. VAEA teal dominant, coral accents for CTAs, 
navy for technical depth sections.